        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.465,
            0.504,
            0.746,
            0.708
          ],
          "content": "Medu and Mishti read ‘thought of the day’ on the school noticeboard every day. Today’s thought, ‘annena jātāni jivanti’, makes them curious. Mishti tells Medu that it is a Sanskrit saying which means ‘food gives life to living beings.’"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.716,
            0.67,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "Let us try to understand the significance of this saying."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.748,
            0.409,
            0.775
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "3.1 What Do We Eat?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.791,
            0.396,
            0.814
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 3.1: Let us record"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.823,
            0.745,
            0.887
          ],
          "content": "All of us eat food every day. Food is an essential component of our daily life. List the food items you have consumed over the week in Table 3.1."
        },
